License map for this distribution
=================================

This is an aggregation, not a single-license operating system.

1. New release tooling: flash.py, flash.cmd, flash.ps1, flash.sh,
   flasher/, image/, tests/, tools/ and the new documentation are licensed
   under the MIT license in LICENSES/MIT.txt, copyright (c) 2026
   Pan-chongyu and contributors. Third-party content is excluded.

2. Adaptation code in research/ is licensed GPL-2.0-only unless a file
   states a different upstream license. Preserve all embedded notices.
   The Linux-derived code and the corresponding Linux source archive are
   governed by their original GPL and SPDX declarations, not by MIT.
   See LICENSES/SyterKit-GPL-2.0.txt for GPL version 2.

3. third_party/fel-emmc/ retains the A523-root MIT license, reproduced
   in LICENSES/A523-root-MIT.txt. SyterKit is GPL-2.0; Arm Trusted
   Firmware is predominantly BSD-3-Clause with its own included notices;
   AIC sources and firmware retain their individual upstream terms.

4. Debian packages retain their respective licenses, available in the
   image at /usr/share/doc/*/copyright. The image itself is not relicensed
   under MIT. Package and source-version inventories accompany releases.

5. Vendor DRAM training and wireless firmware binaries have no source
   provided here. They retain upstream/vendor terms; see THIRD_PARTY.md.
   No blanket open-source license is asserted for those binaries.

6. assets/boot-logo.png and assets/boot-preview.png are artwork supplied
   by the device owner for this boot screen. Original authorship and a
   separate reusable artwork license were not supplied. The MIT/GPL
   grants above do not relicense this artwork.

All upstream copyright notices and license exceptions take precedence
for their respective files.
